  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—the presence of a sure outcome in Lottery B—is explicitly acknowledged and emphasized by the individual ('100%er wahrsch.'). The individual’s justification aligns with preferring the lottery that provides a sure outcome, as they express satisfaction with the guarantee and reject the risk in Lottery A despite its higher potential gain. While there is also an element of risk aversion and evaluation of outcome magnitude, the certainty of the outcome plays a central and explicit role in the reasoning. This matches both the informational basis and the preference rule of the decision reason. Therefore, it is highly likely the individual used this reason in their decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
}

